WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.626
The OWASP Top 10 gives teams a compact way to discuss common application risks, from access control and cryptography to injection, design, configuration, components, identity, integrity, monitoring, and SSRF.

2
00:00:14.626 --> 00:00:24.118
NIST SP 800-53 controls help translate those risks into expectations for governance, engineering, operations, monitoring, and evidence.

3
00:00:24.118 --> 00:00:30.587
A mapping can show where application security activities support broader control objectives.

4
00:00:30.587 --> 00:00:40.924
Security and compliance share responsibility across developers, platform teams, security engineers, administrators, managers, and compliance teams.

5
00:00:40.924 --> 00:00:47.112
The strongest programs make secure behavior repeatable rather than dependent on heroics.

6
00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:51.753
Completion of this course should be treated as awareness training.

7
00:00:51.753 --> 00:01:01.878
It does not prove that an organization has implemented controls, remediated vulnerabilities, or achieved compliance with any specific framework.

8
00:01:01.878 --> 00:01:16.082
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, NIST SP 800-53 references, secure coding checklists, a glossary, a mapping matrix, developer quick-reference sheets, and audit support documentation.

9
00:01:16.082 --> 00:01:19.598
Use this mapping as a discussion and planning aid.

10
00:01:19.598 --> 00:01:23.606
Validate control implementation in the local environment.

11
00:01:23.606 --> 00:01:30.356
Maintain evidence for secure development, monitoring, configuration, and remediation activities.

12
00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:41.677
Selected NIST mappings for this topic include RA-5 - Vulnerability Monitoring and Scanning; SA-11 - Developer Testing and Evaluation; CA-2 - Control Assessments.

